          <h1 class="about__headline">LA Heart. NJ Flair.</h1>

          <div class="about__text">
            <p>Jacob Bellotti is a creative producer and writer in Los Angeles, who has created hit shows for television and written for the EMMY-Winning “RuPaul’s Drag Race.”</p>

            <p>In television, Jacob has created shows like “Owning Manhattan” for Netflix, Crave TV’s “Slaycation!”, and “Bring Back My Girls” for WOWPresentsPlus. He wrote sketches featured on the 28-EMMY winning “RuPaul’s Drag Race” and created challenges for the show. He has produced shows like "American Gladiators" for Prime Video, "Schooled!" for Netflix, and "Citizen Detective" for Sundance.</p>

            <p>Spending 4 years in creative development at World of Wonder Productions, Jacob has also consulted for Hi Mom Productions, worked in talent relations on “America’s Most Wanted” for FOX, and was a talent assistant on “Friends: The Reunion.”</p>

            <p>Beyond developing and producing television, he has written a YA novel, voice acted professionally, performed for the American Comedy Institute in Manhattan, and hosts the popular queer podcast “Let’s Talk About That! With Larry Saperstein and Jacob Bellotti.”</p>
          </div>
        </div>

